ation-hub/v-m-goldschmidt-award"}, {"title": "V. M. Goldschmidt Award (Q1195902)", "url": "https://wikidp.org/Q1195902"}, {"title": "Project Details", "url": "https://cris.bgu.ac.il/en/projects/goldschmidt-2015-support-for-student-participation/"}]}, "The 2015 V. M. Goldschmidt Award went to **Miriam Kastner**, a marine geochemist. The Geochemical Society's awards table lists her for 2015, with citations given by Adina Paytan and Harry Elderfield. 2015 | Miriam Kastner | Adina Paytan and Harry Elderfield | GCA v. 172 pp. 469-470\n\nThe Goldschmidt conference's own medalist page for 2015 says she gave her medal lecture in a session on fluid and solute cycling at subduction zone forearcs. It also describes her as a distinguished professor at Scripps Institution of Oceanography at UC San Diego.\n\nThe award itself is the Geochemical Society's top honor. It recognizes career-long achievement in geochemistry, and it dates to 1972. It honors Victor Moritz Goldschmidt, a pioneer in both those fields."], "durationSeconds": 4.868570333000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01EDh1vFgHuC5q1Qm9qWHyht", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
